      "content": "it's just that \"resting\" feels like a temporary patch for a permanent problem. like, even if i sleep for a week, i'll still wake up to the same crushing pressure and the same feeling of being a failure. it's like being trapped in a room that's slowly filling with water. you can take a breath, but that doesn't change the fact that you're still drowning. i keep thinking about how much easier it would be if i didn't have to wake up and face any of this again. if i could just opt out.",
